From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cataclysm-ios <cataclysm-ios@localhost>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:31:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add iOS platform support

Build with -DCATA_IOS (see the cataclysm-ios port) to run the SDL tiles
build on iPhone and iPad:

- Enter through SDL_main like Android. Read game data from the app
  bundle and keep saves, config and logs in Documents/, which the Files
  app can browse.
- Create a full-screen high-DPI window and lay the terminal out 1:1 in
  pixels inside the safe area (clear of the notch and rounded corners),
  shrinking it above the on-screen keyboard when that is shown. Mouse
  and trackpad positions are mapped from window points to terminal
  pixels.
- Enable the Android touch interface (quick shortcuts, virtual
  joystick, gestures, input context tracking, shortcut persistence)
  on iOS. JNI calls get iOS counterparts: display density, hardware
  keyboard detection, haptics and toasts. SDL on iOS reports touches by
  UITouch address, so fingers are mapped to Android-style indices.
- A keyboard button overlay replaces Android's Back button: tap to
  toggle the keyboard, hold to toggle the shortcut bar.
- Quicksave on focus loss (if enabled) runs inside a background task so
  iOS does not suspend the app mid-save.
- Hide desktop-only display options and size default fonts to the
  screen. Report the iOS version without shelling out.
